    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): [ev-998b2b21608f] is only a bare list item, but it sits in the \"Metrics namespace\" section. That section's intro [ev-1f419676f177] says the listed `cortex_`-prefixed metrics will now start with `loki_`, and that operators can keep the `cortex_` prefix by changing `metrics_namespace` from its default `loki` to `cortex`. So the subject is the metric `cortex_dns_provider_results`. The change is a rename of its prefix to `loki_` (giving `loki_dns_provider_results`). Exposed environments are those that leave `metrics_namespace` at the default, and if their operators do nothing, queries, dashboards and alerts that use the old `cortex_` name will no longer match.",
